  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNDP human rights project - Phase 5</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project &quot;Strengthening multi-stakeholder capacity on and participation in implementing and reporting on international human rights commitments and recommendations made to Viet Nam&quot; aims to strengthen capacity, knowledge, and participation of key stakeholders to meaningfully contribute to implementing, reporting and monitoring of human rights obligations and recommendations made to Viet Nam under UN human rights mechanisms.

Key activities to be implemented in the 5th phase include (i) strengthening capacity and the meaningful engagement of stakeholders in the upcoming UPR Fourth Cycle; (ii) building capacity of youth and civil society organizations (CSO) actors to participate in human rights mechanisms including the UPR; and (iii) building capacity of persons with disabilities (PWDs) and organizations of persons with disabilities (OPDs) to support and monitor implementation of the Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities (CRPD).</narrative>
  </description>
